<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
        Gameplay, generation, and persistence are entirely offline; the only network user is the
        rewarded ad. The three permissions below arrive with the Yandex Mobile Ads SDK and are
        declared here so the merged manifest stays intentional rather than inherited by accident.
        INTERNET and ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE are what an ad request needs. AD_ID is deliberately kept:
        the rewarded placement is served by the Yandex Advertising Network, which uses the
        advertising identifier for frequency capping and fraud checks, so removing it would mean
        denying an advertising integration the app actually has.

        The merge also pulls in AppMetrica's BIND_GET_INSTALL_REFERRER_SERVICE and the AndroidX
        DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION from the SDK's own dependencies, plus the SDK's ad
        activity and its initialization ContentProvider. That provider only bootstraps the SDK;
        consent and `YandexAds.initialize` are driven manually from `YandexAdsInitializer` so the
        privacy state is always set before any ad request.

        The RuStore Pay SDK adds INTERNET (already declared), RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED from its
        analytics dependency, its own payment activity, an initialization ContentProvider, and a
        large `<queries>` block naming the banking apps its payment sheet can hand off to. None of
        that is something the application itself asks for or uses.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />
    <uses-permission android:name="com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID" />

    <application
        android:name=".LogicaApplication"
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.Logica">
        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

        <!--
            How the RuStore Pay SDK initializes itself: its ContentProvider reads both values at
            process start. The console application ID comes from private build configuration and is
            empty in a checkout that has not set it, which only makes the Gem Store unavailable. The
            scheme is the deeplink RuStore returns to after payment.
        -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="console_app_id_value"
            android:value="${rustoreConsoleAppId}" />
        <meta-data
            android:name="sdk_pay_scheme_value"
            android:value="${rustorePayScheme}" />
    </application>
</manifest>
